# A codeaf built on this machine and copied here for `CODEAF_BINARY_FROM=local` image builds (codeaf.Dockerfile).
codeaf-local

# The operator's own settings and secrets: the server key, the hosted-chats secret, the AgentField key and the model
# keys. ./setup.sh writes `.env` from `.env.example`, so a stack that has been started has this file in the tree, and a
# `git add` of the folder would publish every secret in it. The templates stay tracked; a copy of the file under any
# other `.env.*` name (a backup, a second environment) is kept out too. A new template has to be named below on
# purpose, which is the point.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.stub
!.env.stub.hosted
